# Two present reference declarations of two storage types -- `@: box Model 0`, a pointer cell of the graph own's
# pool (POINTER_BASE + its code), and `@: pint int 0`, a pointer cell of int's pool (POINTER_BASE + int's code) --
# in the root's slots 1 and 3, each holding its valid nothing.  The program reads box as unit_at_pointer_cell_catch
# does: the root's `box\v` and a native method's `node\box\v`, each the implicit `interpreter` throw, Entry 7 in both
# modes.  The driver's swap-root-fields 1 3 beside this row exchanges the two cells: each slot then holds a PRESENT
# pointer cell of the other type, which a read admitting any pointer pool took as the valid nothing -- the
# construction promised one exact storage type at each slot, so the swap is X1 at the first read natively ("a
# reference slot holds a pointer cell of another type") and INVALID at the walker's entry load, before any statement.
Model:
    int: v 11
end: Model
@: box Model 0
@: pint int 0
fn: throughBox () int
    int: got 0
    ---
        got: node\box\v
    ---
    catch: interpreter ()
        got: 4
    return: got
int: code 1
---
    code: box\v
---
catch: interpreter ()
    code: code + 2
code: code + throughBox()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
